<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!--
      IsPackable stays INLINE, never hoisted into shared props. The API-baseline coverage gate finds
      shipped projects by TEXT-MATCHING this element, so hoisting it would make this package invisible to
      the gate: it would ship with no baseline and nothing would say so. Media and the mobile pair already
      documented this trap; one duplicated line is the cheaper mistake.
    -->
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Shenora.IO.Compression</PackageId>
    <!--
      ⚠ This text SHIPS to nuget.org and no gate reads it: the D22 domain-word audit sweeps the API
      baselines, so a csproj Description is invisible to it. Two defects lived here until the 2026-08-05
      review — it opened with "Shenora archives", the very name the CHANGELOG records as the defect this
      package was renamed to fix, and it claimed "bounded recursion", which does not exist (zip entries
      are a flat list; the bounds are MaxTotalBytes and MaxEntries). Read it against the code when the
      code changes.
    -->
    <Description>Shenora IO compression: getting files into and out of an archive SAFELY — extraction that refuses any entry escaping its destination, with total-size and entry-count limits, plus a ZIP-backed update source for Shenora.IO's staged updater. Ships no native engine: zip works on the framework alone, and any other format is a seam the application fills.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    net10.0, deliberately not a platform TFM. Nothing here is platform-specific: containment is arithmetic
    over paths and System.IO.Compression is in the shared framework, so the same call site works on all
    three shells. If a format ever needs a native library it arrives as a SEAM the app fills, never as a
    dependency of this package — the same rule D42 applies to media engines.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Shenora.IO, and the edge is REAL rather than declared: ZipUpdateSource implements Shenora.IO's
      IUpdateSource and speaks UpdateManifest/ManifestFile. Added because something crosses it.
      There is deliberately NO Shenora.Core reference: nothing here names a Core type, and Core arrives
      transitively for anyone who needs it. A declared edge nothing crosses is a review finding here.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Shenora.IO\Shenora.IO.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
